
# The panel is its own repository (bwebstudio/telma-dashboard), cloned here
# for convenience. It must never be committed into this one.
dashboard/

# Image and font masters dropped in while redesigning. 42MB that nothing in the
# code imports: the site serves the WebP in web/public/images and the subset
# .woff2 in web/public/fonts, both built from these. Same rule as
# assets/photography above, and this repository is public — the two .zip files
# here are retail type families, which must not be redistributed from it.
web/assets/

# Finder duplicates. Fifteen of these were committed by a careless `git add -A`
# and reached a public repository, where they were stale copies of live files —
# one of them a 2MB video, another a content file complete enough for
# TypeScript to compile it and fail the build on a key the original had grown.
* 2.*

# next build --experimental-build-verify leaves this behind.
.next-verify/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Brand strategy documents. This repository is public: positioning, customer
# psychology, pricing rationale and roadmap do not belong in it. Kept locally.
web/docs/

# Photography masters. ~11MB of lossless PNG that the site never serves — what
# ships is the WebP in web/public/images. Regenerate from the briefs in
# web/lib/images.ts; see assets/photography/README.md.
assets/photography/*.png

# Video master. 6.3MB, still carries the generator's watermark, and the site
# only ever serves the processed files in web/public/video. Kept locally.
assets/video/
